silm:instances_papers_11_base_commutative_diagram_chapters_24_rosetta_stone_cross_domain_sections_05_biologist_entry_point_concrete_anchor_3#morphtrait_obs silm:hasLongDescription "The MorphTrait_obs is morphological-trait observation: small carnivore, retractile claws, body mass below 6 kg -- the morph-classification input. In the paper's apparatus it appears as the symbol 'MorphTrait_obs', a concrete instance grounded in the Mittens domain story; it serves as the anchor whose semantics every diagram, formula, and prose reference back to." .
